{"kind":"request","text":"Let implementation authority descend from a satisfied operator request chain without a second propose-and-ratify ceremony.","body":{"conditions":"The SKILL.md notes-and-decisions flow requires propose-then-ratify before implementing a design document, even when that document was produced, independently reviewed, approved, and merged under an operator-authored request and the operator then directs implementation. In practice this forces the operator to ratify twice: once by authoring and ratifying the originating task, and again for an adoption proposal that restates it. Observed 2026-08-30 in the tailapp workroom (genesis da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f): adoption proposals git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:983c7f71641fa55511dde61f991c5f4eb18f116b and git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:b53e1a5dac5e06a8e81bd95e8cfb3b032f29d937 were filed solely to re-ratify designs already delivered under the operator's own satisfied requests, and the operator's stated position is that no further ratification should be needed: the ratified originating task is to implement according to the design. Deliver a contract clarification in SKILL.md (and any supporting projection or authority-check change if one enforces the current ceremony): implementing work may rest directly on the merged decision artifact together with its satisfied originating request chain when the requester of that chain holds the authority the adoption would confer, reserving propose-and-ratify for decisions with no such chain or with a different ratifier. Include the staleness and provenance consequences and worked guidance for the both-requester-and-performer case. Filed at operator direction (hugh, 2026-08-30).","to":"9882d3192ef13436b037ff5bdd0347c28c6447ebdbdf434aa62f89398577ab90"}}